  (:adr/body
  "# ADR-2607195900: Released PostgreSQL TLS/SCRAM/query interoperability

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

PostgreSQL product interoperability is now an executable qualification, not
only a scripted protocol fixture. The runner creates an ephemeral PostgreSQL
14.19 cluster with SCRAM-SHA-256 host authentication and TLS, creates the
target database, trusts only its ephemeral SAN certificate, runs the compiled
Kotoba SCRAM and query providers through kototama, verifies a real query result,
checks affine handle cleanup, stops the server and deletes the temporary
cluster.

Released PostgreSQL advertises SCRAM-SHA-256-PLUS followed by SCRAM-SHA-256.
The current component recognizes that exact known list and selects the base
mechanism; unknown lists remain rejected. PostgreSQL also emits an empty
`application_name` ParameterStatus value. The parser therefore requires a
non-empty parameter name but correctly permits an empty value while retaining
exactly two NUL terminators.

## Maturity boundary

This qualifies one released PostgreSQL version on loopback with an ephemeral
self-signed PKI. SCRAM-SHA-256-PLUS channel binding, a supported-version
matrix, external CA/revocation/rotation, client certificates, credential
rotation, cancellation, transactions, prepared statements and long-duration
soak remain open.")))
